    feat[SAFE-2]: block-unsupported-documents-and-email-rejections
    
    Admins could approve a tutor request whose identification card or
    certification URL pointed at a file type nobody can verify, and a
    rejection reason was only visible inside the app.
    
    Approval now checks the extension in each verification URL path against
    .pdf, .jpg, .jpeg, .png and .webp before anything is written. A blocked
    approval returns 422 with the offending documents and leaves the request
    pending; rejection is never blocked. URLs without an extension are left
    to the admin. The request list includes documentIssues so the admin page
    can flag files up front.
    
    Rejections are emailed to the applicant after the decision commits, so a
    mail outage cannot undo a recorded decision. The auth and notification
    test mocks gain a stand-in for the new email export.
    
